==============================================================================
THM-527 Thread A: COMPACTNESS for rho*_glob (gap>1/7) -- the 5 claims
==============================================================================

--- (1) continuity of rho*_glob along E(t)=(0..7,t), t:7->9 ---
    max one-step jump (dt=1/300) = 0.018698  (Lipschitz; scales with dt => continuous)

--- (2) degeneracy: collisions RAISE rho*_glob ---
    merges tested: 300; nu DECREASED on merge: 0  (0 => collisions raise the global-witness measure)

--- (3) spread monotonicity: rho*_glob min is at consecutive (small spread) ---
    k=9: rho*_glob for consec vs spread-grown shapes:
      consec [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]: rho*_glob = 0.435374
      [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 20]: rho*_glob = 0.535374
      [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16]: rho*_glob = 0.480612
      [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 50]: rho*_glob = 0.521587
    => consecutive (min spread) gives the SMALLEST rho*_glob (spread RAISES it).

--- (union bound) rho*_glob >= nu_k + cap_k - 1 -- closed-form floor? ---
    k   nu_k(1/7)   cap_k     nu+cap-1   actual-min-rho*_glob
     8  0.9401     0.3815    +0.3216     0.3361
     9  0.8401     0.4943    +0.3344     0.3405
    10  0.7755     0.6044    +0.3799     0.3878
    11  0.6263     0.7253    +0.3516     0.3620
    12  0.5699     0.8571    +0.4270     0.4270
    13  0.4425     1.0000    +0.4425     0.4425
    NOTE: nu+cap-1 is the trivial union LOWER bound (often negative =>
    not enough alone); the ACTUAL rho*_glob is larger because GOOD and
    G_P POSITIVELY correlate (the cluster teeth align with P teeth).
    So the floor needs the overlap (compactness/finite check), not just
    the union bound -- BUT it is robustly POSITIVE (~0.28-0.44).

==============================================================================
